      "author": "Helena ",
      "message": "’Twas the weekend before rotations, his first week in sight,\nAnd all through his schedule, not a moment felt light.\nHis Anki flashcards finished, softly glowing on his screen,\nIn hopes that good sleep might soon slip in between.\n\nHe’s conquered long lectures, each exam and each test,\nWith brilliance and heart, he’s given his best.\nSo before early mornings and long days begin,\nThere’s a night just for him, to unwind and to grin.\n\nA surprise has been planned, just a small little escape,\nFrom the stress and the chaos his days tend to shape.\nWith good food, soft laughs, and a calm, cozy description,\nA night full of love, just his well-earned prescription.\n\nSo come as you are, no need to prepare,\nJust bring that sweet smile I’m lucky to share.\nFor tonight we will pause, celebrate all you’ve done,\nAnd remind you I love you, more than anyone."
