  "letter": {
    "title": "Dear Helena",
    "body": "Dear Helena Bear,\n\nHappy 1 year anniversary!!! One amazing year of giggles, eats, fucks, struggles, parallel play, long commutes, and more. You are the love of my life and my best friend. I have never loved anyone like I love you. \n\nIn the past few months we have had some struggles. The thought of losing you absolutely crushes me. Thank you for pushing me to talk with you and to make a decision together. Watching you offer advice to Sarah and cracking jokes with Mandy, walking with you around Central park, twirling you around my hand on the streets of New York City, and trying to run with you on my back, makes me the happiest boy in the world. So, while some big questions still remain, I feel happy, secure, and confident in our relationship. I love you so much and I want to be with you forever. \n\nAnd it’s funny. Love is so interesting and fickle. I believe that we both view love in similar ways. We want to fully trust our hearts and dive headfirst into the deep end. But our noggins and past experiences warn us to do the opposite. We rationalize, think, and logic to determine if this relationship is the most viable, realistic path for us in the long term. All the while, our poor hearts and souls are hammering away at us, imploring us to remain with each other together. \n\nAnd, sadly, I don’t know what the future holds. What I do know is that I love you and I want to remain together. AND I want us to both be our happiest selves in 50 years. We have yet to figure out what that means for us. And that’s okay. If fully committing to you now means heartbreak down the road, I will choose you every time. I choose you because I want to bask in your presence for as long as I can. I want to dance and sing with you. I want to lay in bed and roll around with you. I want to blow dry your hair and have toilet conversations with you. I want to rant about work and dream about the future with you. I want to joke about Ham, Peaches, and Bertha being our children, with you. I want you. \n\nI made this website to commemorate our year together. It’s a story about how we came to be and the everyday conversations and memories that shaped us. I hope we can continue to add onto it in the many years to come. Montreal, Vancouver, Portugal, my new apartment, California, I want you to be by my side for it all. I don’t want to congratulate you for quitting your job from afar. I don’t want to graduate and send you pictures of the day. I don’t want to change the world and let you know by Linkedin. I want you. \n\nI love you to Pluto and back. \n\nYour Stinky Boy, \n\nJason \n"
  },
